{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n69LWM3nmaNW5ePmBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed \"wholsale\" to \"wholesale\" in one commit, `849b598`, so one `git revert 849b598` undoes it. It changes one line each in `data/2025-10.csv`, `data/2025-11.csv` and `data/2025-12.csv`. `scripts/check.sh` printed `OK`, and a search afterwards found no remaining \"wholsale\".\n\n- **Inbox copy:** `inbox/2025-12.csv` had the same typo, so I fixed it too. Git doesn't track the inbox, so that edit isn't in the commit and a revert won't undo it. Fixing it means re-copying that file won't bring the typo back.\n- **Commit message:** `CLAUDE.md` wants a data month at the start of the message, and this commit covers three months. I used `2025-12`, the latest one. The import log groups by that prefix, so this commit will show up under December. If you'd rather it were grouped differently, say so and I'll reword it.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":315,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":17533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":289,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-38>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:36:51.539Z","request_id":"gen-1794703008-51HXTMvcNj36fZ8VBK5D"}
